# Standing-projection DRIVER gate (ADR-0010 re-bird; closes the Ra4
# standing-projection rung named in the former gates/055 header and V23-T6R
# refutation 2). The offender form -- a forked ledger projection (two chain
# tips maximal in sj:seq for one identity) -- is the inverted companion
# verify/055_standing_projection.unbound.rq (zero-rows-pass,
# offender-reporting per ADR-0010:
# docs/architecture/adr/0010-gate-convention-directory-is-convention.md),
# verbatim former gates/055. The driver witnesses the positive image: every
# WorkOrder projects exactly the standing literal its ledger projection
# carries. One row per order identity.
PREFIX sj: <https://ggen-igniter.dev/ontology/semantic-jira#>
PREFIX dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>
SELECT DISTINCT ?work_order ?identity ?standing WHERE {
  ?work_order a sj:WorkOrder ;
              dcterms:identifier ?identity ;
              sj:standing ?standing .
}
ORDER BY ?identity
